{"title":"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 45","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_45\">Problem 45</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_45&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 45\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b971086a22c0779a30684d8ffa7b4ca0089c066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log 8\\approx .9031$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05dda91d7dadf5ab43b0c02f86274feb00a81e98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log 9\\approx .9542$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />, then the only logarithm that cannot be found without the use of tables is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a849384cfb110732f2ffb2ad36458cfe699f995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\log 17\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\log\\frac{5}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\log 15\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\log 600\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\log .4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"542\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_45&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>While <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1654270f28eaf49ec960b6d7dc75ff8ff42277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log 17 = \\log(8 + 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, we cannot easily deal with the logarithm of a sum. Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is prime, so none of the logarithm rules involving products or differences works. It therefore cannot be found without the use of a table (note: in 1951, calculators were very rare). The correct answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c5166c96e94422f176818ffd64b3c47e329a851f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\log 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"94\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nAs for the rest of the cases: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44a818e38e926d62fd48dc0a60236b2966c5ea57.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log\\frac{5}{4} = \\log\\frac{10}{8} = \\log 10 - \\log 8 = 1 - \\log 8\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"38\" /> can be found; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df7140df5de2bcea8fa51f0a10e54bb1fca686f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log 15 = \\log 3 + \\log 5 = \\frac{1}{2}\\log 3^2 + \\log\\frac{10}{2} = \\frac{1}{2} \\log 9 + \\log 10 - \\log 2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\log 9 + 1 - \\frac{1}{3} \\log 8\\]\" width=\"649\" height=\"37\" /> can be found; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081aee24fd2ac4aaff4d751089188837c6a70a61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log 600 = \\log 100 + \\log 6 = 2 + \\log 2 + \\log 3 = 2 + \\frac{1}{3} \\log 8 + \\frac{1}{2} \\log 9\\]\" width=\"479\" height=\"37\" /> can be found; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397bb0db12625f927b748903f2f78c7f3871215f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log .4 = \\log\\frac{4}{10} = \\log 4 - \\log 10 = 2 \\log 2 - 1 = \\frac{2}{3} \\log 8 - 1\\]\" width=\"449\" height=\"37\" /> can be found.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_45&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME\" title=\"1951 AHSME\">1951 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1951 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1951\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 44\">Problem 44</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_46\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 46\">Problem 46</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl